-- title:
--   Flatness over the base of the edge chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in R$ and let $q$ be a natural number. Consider the quotient $\mathrm{edgeQuot}\,R\,\pi$ of the polynomial ring $R[\xi,\eta]$ in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by the single relation $\xi\eta - \pi$, and in it the element $\mathrm{edgeQuot.discr}\,R\,\pi\,q$, the residue class of the polynomial $\mathrm{edgeDiscr}\,R\,q$. The ring `chartERing R π q` is by definition the localisation of $\mathrm{edgeQuot}\,R\,\pi$ away from that element, i.e. at the multiplicative set of its powers. The assertion is that `chartERing R π q` is flat as an $R$-module, that is, tensoring with it over $R$ preserves injections of $R$-modules. No hypothesis whatsoever is imposed on $R$, on $\pi$ or on $q$; in particular $\pi$ need not be a nonzerodivisor and $q$ need not be a prime power.
--
--   This is the algebraic input for the flatness of the standard edge chart of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane over its base ring: the charts of the levels of Mumford's formal scheme are spectra of quotients of this ring. It is used in the construction of the Mumford glueing data, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky).
